sequenceDiagram
 participant C as Client state
 participant E as ESTS
 Note over C,E: Entry page: retain sFT, sCtx, canary, sessionId, and URLs<br/>Discovery and Remote NGC do not blanket-replace entry state
 C->>E: BeginAuth using MFA-page sFT, sCtx, and SAS canary
 E-->>C: Save SAS SessionId, FlowToken, and Ctx separately
 alt EndAuth GET, retained-state pattern
  C->>E: x-ms-sessionId = MFA-page sessionId
  Note over C,E: x-ms-flowToken and x-ms-ctx = BeginAuth values
  E-->>C: Pending, keep BeginAuth token and context for next poll
 else EndAuth GET, response-state pattern
  C->>E: x-ms-sessionId, x-ms-flowToken, x-ms-ctx
  Note over C,E: from preceding SAS response
  E-->>C: Pending, save returned SAS state for next poll
 else EndAuth POST, code entry
  C->>E: BeginAuth SessionId, FlowToken, Ctx, plus entered code
  E-->>C: Recoverable code rejection can permit another entry
  Note over E,C: keep challenge state, do not repeat BeginAuth
 end
 E-->>C: Successful EndAuth supplies completion FlowToken and Ctx
 C->>E: ProcessAuth: flowToken = successful FlowToken
 Note over C,E: request = successful Ctx, canary = MFA-page canary
 opt ProofUp skip URL advertised
  E-->>C: New ProofUp sFT and canary, sCtx can be absent
  C->>E: Skip resume: flowtoken = ProofUp sFT, canary = ProofUp canary
  Note over C,E: ctx = preceding ProcessAuth request when sCtx is absent
 end
 Note over C,E: FIDO uses a separate bootstrap without blanket state replacement<br/>Keep initiating urlPost, sFT, sCtx, and canary<br/>Bootstrap supplies challenge, cross-domain canary, and completion<br/>sessionId
